					<description><![CDATA[<p>Ominimo Raises Series B Funding At Unicorn Valuation Ominimo raised $22.5 million in its Series B funding round this week, pushing the company to $1.6 billion in valuation within just</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/ominimo-raises-22-5-million-series-b/" data-wpel-link="internal">Ominimo Raises $22.5 Million at $1.6 Billion Valuation</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Ominimo Raises Series B Funding At Unicorn Valuation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ominimo raised $22.5 million in its Series B funding round this week, pushing the company to $1.6 billion in valuation within just two years of launching, making it one of the fastest growing insurtech unicorns in Europe. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike some of Europe’s fastest funded tech startups, which prioritize market size to profit margin, Ominimo has managed to be profitable, as it continues to grow its customer numbers and expand across Europe.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ominimo, based in Budapest and founded in 2024 by Dusan Komar, Dennis Weinbender, Laslo Horvath and Kristina Kozina. It has concentrated on revamping motor insurance through the leveraging of modern data, process automation and AI technology .</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding To Accelerate Licensing And Global Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ominimo is preparing for United States expansion while accelerating long-term international growth and regulatory readiness initiatives. The company currently operates insurance services across Hungary, Poland, the Netherlands, and Sweden with continued expansion. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Operations will soon begin in Belgium and Romania before expanding into Spain, Italy, and France next. Management aims to launch Ominimo&#8217;s insurance services in the United States market by 2027 successfully.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Obtaining its own insurance </span><a href="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/licence" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">licence</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> represents an important strategic objective. At present, Ominimo operates as a managing general agent, handling pricing, customer acquisition, and claims management while partner insurers carry the underwriting risk. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Moving towards a licensed model would allow the company to retain more underwriting profits and gain greater control over product development, although it will also require significantly higher regulatory capital.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI And Data Science Power Insurance Innovation<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203762" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203762" class="size-full wp-image-203762" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/create-a-futuristic-neon-lit-poster-with_aOAqxL_TW9yvNNbrVaSVbA_v-ho9462RciKn7ADGQ7jtw_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI-powered insurance systems analyzing data and automating workflows." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203762" class="wp-caption-text">Ominimo uses AI and data to transform insurance pricing, automation, and operational efficiency. Source: Created by Vnetureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ominimo has differentiated itself by using hundreds of data points to evaluate insurance risk instead of relying on the limited variables commonly used by traditional insurers. This enables the company to price policies more accurately while improving operational efficiency.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its proprietary technology automates much of the insurance process, from pricing and underwriting support to customer service and claims management. The platform continues to learn from customer data, helping improve pricing precision and reduce operational costs over time.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s financial performance reflects this approach. Ominimo&#8217;s annualised gross written premium run rate has increased from €26.3 million in 2024 to approximately €307 million today. It now serves nearly one million customers across multiple European markets while maintaining profitability.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The workforce has expanded rapidly alongside the business. Employee numbers have grown from around 40 people during its early stages to approximately 130 today, with plans to reach 150 employees before the end of the year. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/antares-raises-470m-series-c-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Antares Raises $470M in Series C to Accelerate Military Microreactor Deployment</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Sustainable Growth Strategy Strengthens Market Position</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike many insurtech companies, Ominimo prioritised sustainable growth over aggressive expansion and weak financial operations. Its strategy focused on partnering with incumbent insurers while refining technology and operational capabilities for long-term success. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This approach enabled sustainable growth while building strong partnerships with insurers including Signal Iduna and DA Direkt. These partnerships improved customer experience, pricing models, and the company&#8217;s operational performance across multiple insurance markets globally. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Investors remained confident because Ominimo consistently demonstrated strong business execution throughout its growth history and expansion. Following a $200 million valuation during its 2025 Series A, Ominimo rapidly achieved unicorn status successfully. </span></p>
