					<description><![CDATA[<p>Antares Raises Major Funding For Nuclear Expansion Antares develops advanced nuclear microreactors for military and space applications using highly efficient compact reactor technology. The company has raised $470 million in</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/antares-raises-470m-series-c-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Antares Raises $470M in Series C to Accelerate Military Microreactor Deployment</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Antares Raises Major Funding For Nuclear Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antares develops advanced nuclear microreactors for military and space applications using highly efficient compact reactor technology. The company has raised $470 million in Series C financing supporting commercialisation through equity and debt. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding round was co-led by Paradigm and Caffeinated Capital with multiple strategic investors participating together. Additional investors included Point72 Ventures, Shine Capital, Industrious Ventures, and several other institutional investment firms globally. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The financing included $370 million in equity alongside $100 million in debt capital for commercial expansion. Antares will use the funding to transition from reactor demonstrations toward full commercial deployment across markets. </span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Commercial Microreactor Rollout</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding follows Antares achieving a significant technical milestone earlier this year in </span><a href="https://www.energy.gov/ne/articles/nuclear-101-how-does-nuclear-reactor-work" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">nuclear reactor</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> development. Antares became the first privately engineered non-light-water nuclear reactor demonstrating criticality in over forty years. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Mark-0 reactor achieved this milestone at Idaho National Laboratory in the United States successfully this year. The company will use the capital to develop its electricity-producing Mark-1 reactor expected by 2027 successfully. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Funding will also improve manufacturing capabilities and production processes supporting existing defence customers across government programmes. This includes work supporting the U.S. Air Force’s Advanced Nuclear Power for Installations Program initiatives. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding also supports the U.S. Navy’s expeditionary power programme and related advanced energy projects. Chief executive officer Jordan Bramble said Antares has established proof-of-concept for its innovative nuclear technology successfully. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">He said the company will now focus on preparing for commercial implementation and broader market deployment. The investment supports collaboration with government partners building reliable power systems requiring no refuelling for six years.</span></p>
<h2><b>Microreactors Target Defence And Energy Security<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203758" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203758" class="size-full wp-image-203758" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/create-a-futuristic-neon-lit-poster-with_lSSEKWuuUm2e_-hEnQ08Og_6mbSSFQQSxG035eJqfKI5w.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing a compact nuclear reactor powering remote defence or space systems." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203758" class="wp-caption-text">Antares develops autonomous nuclear microreactors for resilient, long-term energy in defence and remote environments. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Antares develops compact nuclear microreactors designed to provide continuous electricity in locations where conventional energy infrastructure is difficult to maintain. The systems are intended for military bases and space applications that require dependable long-term power.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s reactors are designed to operate autonomously for years while reducing dependence on vulnerable fuel supply chains. This has become increasingly important as governments seek more resilient energy infrastructure for defence operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">According to the company, the latest funding will help meet the timeline outlined in Executive Order 14299, which calls for an operational reactor at a domestic military installation by September 2028.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/candid-health-raises-120m-ai-revenue-cycle-management/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Candid Health Raises $120M to Expand AI-Powered Healthcare Revenue Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Investors Back Proven Technical Progress</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Investors cited Antares&#8217; recent engineering achievements as a key reason for supporting the company. Paradigm highlighted the successful operation of the company&#8217;s factory-built microreactor and its transition towards large-scale deployment.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Caffeinated Capital also pointed to Antares&#8217; progress in reactor development, customer acquisition and supply chain strategy. The firm believes the company&#8217;s focus on defence customers and long-term operational reliability positions it well within the growing advanced nuclear sector.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Founded in 2023, Antares has rapidly expanded its operations across facilities in California, Idaho and South Carolina. The company is developing nuclear energy systems that can provide secure, long-duration power for defence and strategic applications while reducing reliance on traditional energy infrastructure.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/antares-raises-470m-series-c-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Antares Raises $470M in Series C to Accelerate Military Microreactor Deployment</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
