					<description><![CDATA[<p>Spanish tech star Multiverse Computing has hit a massive financial milestone. Multiverse Computing Raises $570 million in a landmark Series C funding round to scale its energy-efficient software globally.  Co-led</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/multiverse-computing-raises-570-million-for-expansion/" data-wpel-link="internal">Multiverse Computing Raises $570 Million in Series C Funding for Global Expansion</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Spanish tech star Multiverse Computing has hit a massive financial milestone. Multiverse Computing </span><a href="https://x.com/MultiverseCompu/status/2081637171669152079" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">Raises $570 million</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> in a landmark Series C funding round to scale its energy-efficient software globally. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Co-led by Forgepoint Capital International, BNPP Solar Impulse Venture Fund, and Bullhound Capital, the deal values the San Sebastián firm at $1.7 billion pre-money. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Additional backers include HP Inc., Orange Ventures, Scania Invest, and Santander. The massive influx of capital will help the team scale its quantum-inspired compression tech across major international markets.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiverse To Break the High-Energy AI Infrastructure Barrier</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203753" style="width: 944px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203753" class="size-full wp-image-203753" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Multiverse-Computing.jpg" alt="Multiverse Computing quantum AI model compression diagram showing data shrinking for edge devices." width="934" height="568" /><p id="caption-attachment-203753" class="wp-caption-text">Multiverse Computing Founders</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For years, mainstream tech companies accepted a costly rule: powerful artificial intelligence requires massive data centers and enormous amounts of power. Multiverse Computing built its reputation by challenging that idea. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Co-founders Enrique Lizaso and Dr. Román Orús created CompactifAI to change how businesses run software models. CompactifAI uses tensor networks to compress large language models. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This software shrinks model sizes by 80% to 95%. However, it maintains the overall accuracy. That means complex tools can run on local processors without racking up gigantic electricity bills. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">CEO Enrique Lizaso emphasized that companies no longer need to depend solely on expensive cloud data centers to get top performance.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/ropedia-raises-30m-pre-a-funding-scale-physical-ai-infrastructure/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Ropedia Raises $30M To Scale Physical AI Data Infrastructure</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Powering On-Device Intelligence from Edge to Cloud</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Running software on local hardware offers huge benefits for modern enterprises. Relying entirely on remote cloud servers causes latency issues, costs a fortune, and creates serious privacy risks. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiverse solves this bottleneck by putting compressed intelligence directly onto edge devices. Smartphones, autonomous vehicles, industrial cameras, and satellites can now execute complex tasks without an active internet connection. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Major companies like Bosch, Telefónica, Allianz, and Bank of Canada already deploy these solutions to streamline daily operations. The software also features an intelligent router. It decides whether a task should run locally on a phone or jump to a cloud server, saving processing power every step of the way.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/atoms-raises-1-7-billion-robotics-automation/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Atoms Raises $1.7 Billion To Automate Physical Industries</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Fueling Global Scale and Sovereign Tech Infrastructure</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The $570 million Series C cash injection will aggressively power Multiverse’s global growth strategy. The company is setting up dedicated hubs across North America, the Middle East, East Asia, and Southeast Asia. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The goal is to bring green computing tools straight to local commercial hubs. A large portion of the capital will also support sovereign AI projects. Governments and enterprise clients want software platforms hosted on their own soil to comply with strict regional laws. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Multiverse provides an operating system layer that helps regional gigafactories run efficiently without relying on foreign cloud providers. Commercial momentum backs this strategic push. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Since its Series B round in 2025, Multiverse grew annualized revenue more than tenfold. Its Q1 2026 sales surged 96 times higher year-over-year, making it one of Europe’s fastest-growing deep-tech operations.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/genius-ai-raises-44-million-series-d-service-economy/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Genius AI Raises $44M Into AI In-Person Service Economy</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/multiverse-computing-raises-570-million-for-expansion/" data-wpel-link="internal">Multiverse Computing Raises $570 Million in Series C Funding for Global Expansion</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
