<h3><strong>The Concept of LTV (Loan-to-Value)</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The loan-to-value ratio determines how much capital you can borrow. It compares the requested loan amount against your deposited collateral. Therefore, a 50% ratio means borrowing half of your collateral&#8217;s value.</span></p>
<h3><strong>Margin Calls and Liquidations</strong></h3>
